A||N||7||newfie||T-top Q's||||5||
Z||000000||newfie||11-08-2000||08:01 PM||||I was just wondering what Fiero's were made with t-bar roof.  What models? years? general info.  Also is there any kits to make a normal roof Fiero to a t-top.  Is there any structural differences in the body in a t-top for extra support.  I know that most t-top cars had extra supports in the main frame.  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||11-08-2000||08:16 PM||||The '88 model year was the only one that was offered with 'factory' T-Tops. It could be ordered on any model.<BR>There are no other structural differences besides the 'H' bar.<BR>There were some kits still available this last spring but I do believe that they are now gone!<BR>You may still be able to find some in a salavage yard 'some where over the rainbow' (LOL)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||11-08-2000||08:27 PM||||To add to what Indiana said, you could try contacting Tim at fieroparts.com, he might still have some t-top kits left.<P>Not sure what type of "general info." you are looking for but I am sure we can help you out....<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||pollock||11-09-2000||12:26 PM||||I am STILL working on putting Ttops in a non-ttop fiero.  I bought a used assembly from a guy on this board.  <P>I've done a lot of mods to various cars, and i'd rank this as pretty hard.  If you don't have a lot of trim experience, shy away.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tom88gt||11-09-2000||01:27 PM||||"factory" T-tops only available in 88.  I think about 1200 were done.  Earlier year t-tops are after market installs by C&C, which is who did the 88 "factory" jobs.  I would estimate probably less than 2000 total t-tops ever do.  Subtract the % of Fieros in junk yards and you get a pretty good idea of their rarity.  I enjoy my 88 but it does leak when it rains and weather stripping is impossible to find.  I still think a fair trade off over a drier sunroof model.  I do have a complete spare t-top roof of an 85 SE.  I am saving it for spare parts or incase my 88 is stolen or the roof gets crushed somehow.  But I would consider selling the complete roof if someone wants to try to convert their hard top.  Actually appears to be pretty straight forward, just measure several times and cut once.  When I removed some of the 85 roof frame pieces, it was apparant that the t-top is designed to install without a precision cutting of the roof.  But your best bet is to locate a junkyard top your self, pull the headliner and evaluate the install and whether or not you have tha skills to swap it. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||007DOUG||11-09-2000||10:44 PM||||Here's a REALLY general pic series of a T-top install in my GT: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/FIEROWAREHOUSE/ttopinstall.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/FIEROWAREHOUSE/ttopinstall.html</A> <P>The hardest part (next to finding replacement weatherstrips) is flexing your fiero frame. Most guys place concrete blocks under the middle of their fiero and let it sag.<P>My install was performed by The Fiero Factory. If you purchase a t-top section such as Tom's, they can install it for you using original C&C tools. <P>------------------<BR>5 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>84 SE<BR>86 SE V6 153K<BR>2 86 GT's<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>2 88 GT's (twins)<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tom88gt||11-10-2000||10:10 AM||||I'll have to recant on the t-top offer.  I went back to the junkyard.  The guy that I had arranged to cut the top off is no longer working there.  I did get all the "bolt-on" stuff earlier (glass, end caps, trim, etc) which is all I originally wanted.  Just not the "H" frame yet.  Well, the car is now on the "crush" pile awaiting its fate.  I didn't see it but it's probably under a stack of cars so the H frame is likely damaged.  <P>If you really really want the whole top, I can still try.  But your better off seeking another top.  A while ago, there was someone, in CA I think, who was selling complete junkyard tops for $500 (which is what I would sell for).  Keep in mind, I have come across a couple of brand new, complete t-top kits in the $2000 range.  More than I would pay, unless I had a pristene, low mileage 88GT and was solidly in the upper middle class income range.  But then I might be driving a C-4 Vette...  ||||reg||9
Z||000007||fieroparts.com||11-10-2000||03:07 PM||||Hi  we have 4 new kit in stock.<BR>Check out our web site at <A HREF="http://www.fieroparts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroparts.com</A> <P>then give us a call at 1-800-ALL-FIEROS<BR>1-800-255-3437<P>Thanks Tim<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroparts.com/ttop/ttopkit1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroparts.com/ttop/ttopkit1.jpg</A> <P><BR>||||reg||7
